    "number": 183,
    "title": "Refresh the work guide to current issue state",
    "body": "## Purpose\n\nThis is an intentional guide revision before public publication, which the owner requested. The saved inputs are refreshed to current GitHub state, and every status statement in the guide now matches the trackers. The owner asked for no stale blockers or statuses.\n\n## Snapshot\n\n- Backlog snapshot `2026-09-23T07:19:18Z`: 91 open issues (Hub 59, Nanoleaf 16, Pixoo 16) across 12 guides.\n- History is read from paginated read-only `gh api` calls at heads Hub `1338c03`, Nanoleaf `cbb9485` and Pixoo `c81bc31`. Every previously recorded entry is unchanged.\n- Base is `main` `1338c03`. It includes #174, #176, #177 and #180.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Coverage:**\n  - Closed: H16, H64, H158, H172, N21, N43 and N70. Each is now a direct read, so its link shows Completed.\n  - Newly placed: H175 and H178 go to Controls + music. H179, H181 and H182 go to Shared Codex integration. P68 goes to Development workflow.\n- **Rows and notes rewritten** where they described closed, merged or unblocked work as open, pending or blocked:\n  - Tidbyt: #16 is delivered and absorbed #15. The next steps are #19 and then #21.\n  - Nanoleaf: #42 was folded into #43, which is delivered. #21's findings are delivered.\n  - N30: #64 is delivered.\n  - iPhone sources: #158 is delivered.\n  - Atlas: #172 is delivered.\n  - Guide rules: #70 is done and P68 is next.\n  - The general-control, H56 and H152 wording now reflects delivered #31, #151 and #153.\n  - PC-lighting follow-up count, Pixoo #12 baseline wording, and the H65, H67 and Tidbyt prerequisite notes.\n- **Reading paths and cards:**\n  - Next steps are updated for five guides.\n  - The closed H15 and N42 parallel cards are removed, and an H19 card is added.\n  - The overview's \"Independent work\" card and parallel-boundary line are updated.\n- **Roadmap nodes** no longer list closed issues.\n- **Diagrams:**\n  - The Nanoleaf Linux runtime is re-rendered as installed (#54 and #55 are complete).\n  - The owner-migration, desktop-input and preset metadata no longer report pending installation or open prerequisites.\n  - All 9 diagrams passed Archify's 9/9 checks with 0 errors and 0 warnings. Only `arch-nanoleaf-linux` has new viewer bytes.\n- **Checks:** the status examples in `test_maintenance.py` and `check_guide.cjs` now use stable current issues: H50 for in review with a blocked label, and N46 for blocked.\n\nThese tracker changes were made separately, with the owner's approval. They are not part of this diff. A stale `blocked` label was removed, with a comment, from Hub #11, #19, #23, #25, #26, #65, #67, #154, #155 and #173, Nanoleaf #15 and #44, and Pixoo #17. Every recorded blocker for these is closed. Issues whose `blocked` label has no recorded reason (N12–N14, N16, N19, N20, H50) are unchanged; the guide shows those chips as Blocked, and H50 as In review · blocked.\n\nA read-only audit agent checked every guide intro, row, note, reading path and card against live GitHub. All of its stale findings are applied.\n\n## Validation on `6731185`\n\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/build_guide.py`, then a rebuild with `git diff --exit-code -- docs/work-guide/outputs`: no drift.\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/test_maintenance.py`: 9 tests OK.\n- `node docs/work-guide/work/check_guide.cjs` (Playwright, Chromium headless shell 1243, Node 24.20.0): `errors: []`, 0 external requests.\n- `python3 docs/system-design/check.py`: OK. The atlas embeds D2 and D3, which are unchanged here.\n- `index` HTML SHA-256: `3ed7fa1db01c73b717f1c5fb03175195bbdcc3e0bec457217397045b8a6aa897`.\n\n## CI and UI\n\n- Every changed path is under `docs/work-guide/`, so the [guide-only CI exception](docs/sdlc.md#guide-only-ci-exception) applies. Both Depot workflows `paths-ignore` this folder. The exception readbacks will be recorded on this PR.\n- The change is guide UI and content only, which is exempt from human UI approval under the SDLC UI approval scope. Independent Standards and Specification reviews are still required.\n\nPublic publication to `jimmie-potts/agent-device-guide` follows in a linked PR after merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
    "state": "open",
